# README.md is NOT ignored: pyproject.toml declares `readme = "README.md"`, so the build
# backend needs it present to generate package metadata. Excluding it made
# `COPY pyproject.toml README.md ./` fail — dropping it from the COPY instead would just move
# the failure into `pip install .`.
